  "Question": "Alicia earns \\(\\$20\\) per hour, of which \\(1.45\\%\\) is deducted to pay local taxes. How many cents per hour of Alicia’s wages are used to pay local taxes?",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(0.0029\\)",
    "B": "\\(0.029\\)",
    "C": "\\(0.29\\)",
    "D": "\\(2.9\\)",
    "E": "\\(29\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "E",
  "Solution": "Convert the wage to cents first so that the calculation gives the requested unit. Since one dollar is \\(100\\) cents, Alicia earns \\(20\\cdot100=2000\\) cents per hour. Also, \\(1.45\\%=0.0145\\), so her hourly tax is\n\\[\n2000\\cdot0.0145=29\n\\]\ncents. The answer is \\(29\\) cents per hour, choice \\(\\mathrm{E}\\).",
